@startuml notifications_inbox
title Inbox and notification preferences
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "hermes (CLI / TUI)" as Client
participant "hermes-notification-service" as HNS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Update notification preferences ==
User -> Client : Configure users / workspaces / documents category
Client -> HNS : UpdateNotificationPreferences(category, enabled, session)
HNS -> DB : Save preferences for authenticated user only
HNS --> Client : Updated preferences
note over HNS
  Preferences affect future notifications, not events or existing inbox items.
end note

== Read inbox from CLI or TUI ==
User -> Client : Open inbox or run hermes inbox list
Client -> HNS : ListInbox(category?, unread_only?, cursor), UnreadCount
HNS -> DB : Select recipient inbox; hide inaccessible targets\nexcept minimal deletion/removal notices
HNS --> Client : Items, cursor, mark-all boundary and unread count
Client --> User : Show inbox

== Open a notification target ==
User -> Client : Open notification
Client -> HNS : GetTarget(notification_id, session)
HNS -> DB : Validate recipient and current target permissions
alt Target accessible
  HNS --> Client : Document, invitation or profile
  Client -> HNS : MarkRead(notification_id)
  HNS -> DB : Set read_at if not already set
else Target deleted or access revoked
  HNS --> Client : Target unavailable; no content disclosed
end

== Mark notifications as read ==
User -> Client : Mark one item or all listed items as read
Client -> HNS : MarkRead(id) / MarkAllRead(list_boundary)
HNS -> DB : Validate recipient; update read_at up to the boundary
HNS --> Client : Updated unread count
note over Client, DB
  New arrivals beyond the boundary remain unread.
  TUI polls for updates; one-shot CLI exits.
  Inbox items persist even when no client is running.
end note
@enduml
